.TH LIBMPQ__PATCH_SIGN 3 2026-09-29 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__patch_sign \- configure signing for a staged patch archive
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__patch_sign(mpq_patch_s *patch, uint32_t signature_type, const uint8_t *private_key, size_t private_key_size);"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Configures \fBLIBMPQ_SIGNATURE_WEAK\fP or \fBLIBMPQ_SIGNATURE_STRONG\fP
signing on an active patch writer. The operation delegates to the ordinary
archive signing implementation. Configure each type at most once before
libmpq__patch_finish(3); ordinary MPQ patches may configure both types.
The existing archive writer generates signatures during finalization.
.PP
MPQE-wrapped patches support weak signatures but reject external strong
signatures with \fBLIBMPQ_ERROR_FORMAT\fP, matching archive signing behavior.
This call does not consume the patch handle, including when configuration
fails. It does not modify the base archive.
.PP
After finish, open the patch with the ordinary MPQ or authenticated MPQE
reader. Use libmpq__archive_signatures(3) and libmpq__archive_verify(3)
to inspect and verify its signatures. No separate patch verification API exists.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns \fBLIBMPQ_SUCCESS\fP or an existing negative libmpq error.
.SH ERRORS
A NULL patch returns \fBLIBMPQ_ERROR_EXIST\fP. Invalid types, keys, duplicate
configuration, and unsupported MPQE strong signing return
\fBLIBMPQ_ERROR_FORMAT\fP. Writer lifecycle and capacity errors may propagate
from libmpq__archive_sign(3).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmpq__patch_begin (3),
.BR libmpq__patch_begin_mpqe (3),
.BR libmpq__patch_finish (3),
.BR libmpq__archive_sign (3),
.BR libmpq__archive_signatures (3),
.BR libmpq__archive_verify (3)
